## 2.2. Preparation of ZIF-8 and ZIF-8/CS composite gel
## 2.2.1. Synthesis of ZIF-8
\(\mathrm{Zn}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\) \(_{(0.6\mathrm{~g)}}\) was dissolved in \(50~\mathrm{mL}\) of deionized water, and \(2.6~\mathrm{g}\) of 2-H-MeIM was dissolved in \(37.4~\mathrm{mL}\) of deionized water, respectively. Then, the two solutions were mixed under stirring and kept \(80\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(12~\mathrm{{h}}\) . The resultant powders were collected by centrifugation and thoroughly washed with deionized water. The product was dried by a freeze dryer (Shanghai Bilang Instrument Manufacture Co. Ltd., Shanghai China) at \(-56\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) .
## 2.2.2. Synthesis of ZIF-8/CS composite gel
Firstly, \(\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}/\mathrm{CS}\) solution was prepared. CS powder was dissolved in \(2\;\mathrm{vol.}\%\) acetic acid aqueous solution to prepare CS solution \((0.5\;w t.\%)\) . Then, \(0.6\,g\) of \(\mathrm{Zn(NO_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6H_{2}O}\) , as the source of Zinc, was added to \(40\,\mathrm{mL}\) of the as prepared chitosan solution. Secondly, a mixed coagulation solution was prepared, containing both NaOH and 2-H-MeIM, with the concentration of \(5.0\;\;w t.\%\) and \(6.6\;\;w t.\%\) , respectively. Thirdly, the composite gel was formed. The mixed coagulation solution was added dropwise into the \(\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}/\mathrm{CS}\) solution, until CS had been completely precipitated. The solution and precipitation were transferred into an autoclave to continue the reaction at \(80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(12\,\mathrm{{h}}\) . The products were thoroughly washed with deionized water.
## 2.3. Composite paper preparation
Paper-sheets with target basis weight of \(60~\mathrm{g}\cdot\mathrm{m}^{-2}\) were prepared using a laboratory sheet former. The wet sheets were pressed according to the TAPPI test method T 201 sp-95 and then air dried at \(25\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) and 50 \(\%\) relative humidity. Method A: the as prepared ZIF-8 powder was added as fillers without any chemical reagent, and the total dry weight of cellulose fiber in the pulp was \(1.9\,g\) . Method B: the as prepared ZIF-8 powder was added as fillers with cationic retention aid (CPAM), and the parameters of the pulp were controlled as the same in Method A. Method C: ZIF-8 was in situ deposited on a paper sheet (prepared in advance, basis weight of \(60~\mathrm{g}\cdot\mathrm{m}^{-2}\) ) according to literature (Su et al., 2018). Method D: ZIF-8/CS composite gel was added in the pulp and mixed thoroughly. The pulp containing composite gel was then used to paper-sheets. The dry weight ratio of CS to cellulose fiber was 1:9, while the total dry weight of CS and cellulose was controlled as the value of cellulose in Method A.
