The strength properties (tensile index) of the paper-sheets were determined using the L&W C0062 Tensile Strength Tester (Sweden), according to standard GB/T 22898-2008. The uniformity of the composite paper sheet was indicated by the evenness index measured by a Paprican micro-scanner. The paper-sheet properties were all determined according to the standards.
## 2.6. Material characterization
The microstructure of ZIF-8, ZIF-8/CS composite gel and composite paper made by different methods were all observed by Scanning Electron Microscope (SEM, HITACHI S-4800). Samples were gold-sprayed for conductance. The diameters of ZIF-8 crystals were analyzed statistically by software Image View. The X-ray diffraction (XRD) tests of all samples were performed using a D/max 2200PC X-ray diffractometer \((40\,\mathrm{kV},20\,\mathrm{mA})\) with a \(\mathrm{Cu}\,\mathrm{K}\alpha\) anode from \(5^{\circ}\) to \(40^{\circ}\) and a scanning rate of 2 degree \(\mathrm{min}^{-1}\). The attenuated total reflection Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (ATR-FTIR) spectra of samples were obtained with a Bruker Victory 22 spectrophotometer (Bruker, Germany) in the wavenumber range of \(500{-}4000\,\mathrm{cm}^{-1}\).
## 2.7. Gas adsorption ability
Gas adsorption isotherms were obtained by a Gemini VU2390 automated apparatus (Micromeritics, USA) at \(77\,\mathrm{K}\). Samples were degassed by \(\mathrm{N}_{2}\) blowing at \(105\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(1\,\mathrm{~h~}\) before \(\mathrm{N}_{2}\) adsorption testing. The Brunauer-Emmett-Teller specific surface area (BETSSA) of ZIF-8, ZIF-8/CS composite gel and composite paper were calculated by \(\mathrm{N}_{2}\) adsorption isotherms at relative vapor pressures of \(0.01{-}0.3\;\mathrm{MPa}\).
## 2.8. Filtration performance
Filtration tests were performed by a LZC-K1 filter tester (Suzhou Huada Filter Technology Co., Ltd, China) at \(28\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) and the relative humidity of \(40\ \%\) . Diethyl hexyl sebacate (DEHS) aerosol particles were generated by a nebulizer, with the diameter of \(0.3\ \upmu\mathrm{m}\) , \(0.5\ \upmu\mathrm{m}\) , \(1.0\ \upmu\mathrm{m}\) , \(2.5\;\upmu\mathrm{m}\) , \(5.0\;\upmu\mathrm{m}\) and \(10.0\ \upmu\mathrm{m}\) , respectively. The aerosol particles flowed through the composite paper with the flow rate of \(32\,\mathrm{L}\cdot\mathrm{min}^{-1}\) . The total measuring time and effective testing area are \(^{10\,\mathrm{~s~}}\) and \(132.7\ \mathrm{cm}^{2}\) , respectively. The filtration efficiency \(\eta\) and pressure drop were evaluated using the following equations:
\[
\eta=1\frac{C_{downstream}}{C_{upstream}}
\]
The air permeability values of the paper sheets were measured using a L&W 166 Air Permeance Tester (Sweden) according to GB/T 22819-2008.
## 2.9. Antibacterial performance and photocatalytic disinfection
Gram-negative Escherichia coli (E. coli) was used as a model bacterium to studied antibacterial activities of the composite paper. The antibacterial activities were evaluated by the inhibition zone testing (Ma, Zhang, Nie, Tan, Yang et al., 2019). Luria–Bertani (LB) broth medium and all Petri dishes were disinfected at \(100\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(15\ \mathrm{min}\) in an autoclave, respectively. Then \(15\ \mathrm{mL}\) of the LB medium was uniformly poured into the Petri dishes with a diameter of \(90\ \mathrm{mm}\) and cooled down to solidification at room temperature. Subsequently, E. coli suspension contain \(100\ \upmu\mathrm{L}\) \((108\ \mathrm{CFU\ mL^{-1}})\) was evenly spread over the medium. The samples with a diameter of \(13\ \mathrm{mm}\) were carefully placed in the dishes and incubated at \(30\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(24\ \mathrm{h}\) and \(48\ \mathrm{h}\), respectively. The photocatalytic antibacterial activity of the composite paper was examined. A lamp was employed as light source with optical power density fixed at \(100\ \mathrm{mW\cdot cm^{-2}}\) (1 sun) to simulate sunlight irradiation. There were a series of experiments conducted with light while others were conducted in the dark with the same situations. Finally, the dishes were taken photos and the diameter of inhibition zone was measured. All the experiments were repeated for three times.
