## 3. Result and discussion
MOFs were in situ formed in CS gel and subsequently transformed into MOFs-paper material. This strategy was evaluated in aspects of MOFs retention, paper properties and potential in air pollution control.
## 3.1. Characterization of ZIF-8 and ZIF-8/CS composite gel
ZIF-8 was prepared by hydrothermal method as confirmed by XRD result (Fig. 1a), FTIR result (Fig. 1b) and SEM observation (Fig. 1c) (Li et al., 2019). The as-obtained crystals showed typical rhombic dodecahedral morphology, and the average diameter of ZIF-8 crystals prepared by direct hydrothermal method was \(1.65\ \upmu\mathrm{m}\) (standard deviation 0.18).
ZIF-8/CS composite gel was prepared by hydrothermal synthesis coupled with the gelation of CS (Scheme 1c). ZIF-8 crystals were in situ synthesized in the CS gel, also confirmed by XRD result, FTIR result and SEM observation. The small peak at \(2\theta=20^{\circ}\) in the XRD pattern (Fig. 1a) was attributed to the form II crystals of CS (Wang, Nie, Qin, Hu, & Tang, 2016), and the absorption peak at \(1378\ \mathrm{cm}^{-1}\) in the FTIR spectra (Fig. 1b) was attributed to the amide band III of CS (Nie, Wang, Zhang, & Hu, 2015). ZIF-8 crystals with rhombic dodecahedral shape were successfully generated and densely laid in the CS gel (Fig. 1d). It is noteworthy that the average diameter of ZIF-8 crystals in the composite gel was \(416.6\ \mathrm{nm}\) (standard deviation 55.1), which was lower than the crystals synthesized without CS (Fig. 1c, d). This indicated that the ZIF-8 crystals in the composite gel had external lager specific surface area, which was favorable for subsequent applications. This phenomenon could be attribute to the influence of CS which possibly provide extra crystal nucleus during the crystallization of ZIF-8 (Asenath-Smith, Li, Keene, Zhi, & Estroff, 2012).
In addition to success synthesis, it is also important to evaluate whether the CS affected the yield of ZIF-8. After comparison, the yield of ZIF-8 in the composite gel was \(90.24\ \%\) the value of the synthesis without CS (Table S1), indicating the existence of CS did not exert significant impact on the yield of ZIF-8.
## 3.2. Retention of ZIF-8 in the composite paper
